  /**
   * Sync transactions (change feed)
   *
   * <p>Returns what changed in a connection's transactions since a <code>cursor</code>: <code>added</code>, <code>modified</code> and <code>removed</code> (with a <code>reason</code>), across all its accounts. An empty cursor returns every current transaction as <code>added</code> and sets <code>reset: true</code>: replace your copy with it instead of adding to it.
   *
   * <p>The first read is a true snapshot. A first read (no cursor, or the read after <code>reset</code>) returns every transaction the connection had when the read started, each exactly once as <code>added</code>, in its current state, even if a sync runs while you page. Changes made while you were paging arrive in the next read from <code>next_cursor</code>: a transaction you already received comes again as <code>modified</code>, and a new one as <code>added</code>. Apply <code>modified</code> as an upsert by <code>id</code>, and ignore a <code>removed</code> id you do not have. All pages of one read reflect the same point in time. Keep paging with <code>page_token</code> while <code>has_more</code> is <code>true</code>, and store <code>next_cursor</code> only after a response with <code>has_more: false</code>. If paging fails midway, restart from the cursor you had stored.
   *
   * <p>The change log is replayable for 90 days. An older cursor answers <code>410 cursor_expired</code> with <code>bootstrap: true</code>: start again from an empty cursor. Stored history is never aged out while the connection exists. A booked pending transaction appears in <code>added</code> and the pending one in <code>removed</code> with <code>reason: pending_booked</code>. Webhook <code>bank.data.updated</code> tells you when to call.
   *
   * <p>Needs an API key with the Bank data permission (<code>bank-data</code>): read for this operation. A key with full access does not include it: grant it explicitly when you create the key, or the call answers <code>403 bank_data_access_denied</code>. A sandbox application reads its Test Bank data with the key alone. A request without an API key (client credentials) is refused on raw data with the same <code>403</code>.
   *
   * <p>{@code GET /v3/bank/connections/{id}/transactions/sync/}
   *
   * @param id The connection id.
   * @param params the request parameters
   * @param options per-request options that override the client options
   * @return the response body
   */
  public BankTransactionChanges syncTransactions(String id, BankSyncTransactionsParams params, RequestOptions options) {
    return client.execute(syncTransactionsRequest(id, params), options, SYNC_TRANSACTIONS_RESPONSE).data();
  }

